-- ccc11-investigation.l4 -- Part VIII.1, sections 320.27 to 320.3 (Investigative Matters: demands, samples, warrants) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A power of a peace officer, an evaluating officer or a justice ("may ... if") answers JUST TRUE when every gate of the text holds and NOTHING when one does not (ruling of 2026-11-12: a grant is not
-- turned into a bar; each such site is a fork line in NOTES.md, fork F8). A duty answers JUST FALSE where the text's own "if" is unmet. "Peace officer", "evaluating officer", "justice", "qualified technician",
-- "qualified medical practitioner", "approved screening device" and the other defined terms are taken as inputs named for the section that defines them, typed MAYBE BOOLEAN, so a NOTHING among them is carried through.
-- Reasonable grounds, and "in the officer's opinion", are plain facts about the officer's state of mind: the person states what they can.

-- Line 6351: the division heading "Investigative Matters": inert (reason 1, a heading).
-- src:6351 | Investigative Matters
§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.27: testing for the presence of alcohol or a drug`

-- (1): "If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that a person has alcohol or a drug in their body and that the person has, within the preceding three hours, operated a conveyance, the
-- peace officer may, by demand, require the person to comply with the requirements of either or both of paragraphs (a) and (b) in the case of alcohol or ... (a) and (c) in the case of a drug".
-- One function per paragraph: the officer's power to demand THAT requirement. "Within the preceding three hours" is a period the text fixes in its own words (counted as at most three hours).
-- src:6352 | Testing for presence of alcohol or drug
-- src:6353 | 320.27 (1) If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that a person has alcohol or a drug in their body and that the person has, within the preceding three hours, operated a conveyance, the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to comply with the requirements of either or both of paragraphs (a) and (b) in the case of alcohol or with the requirements of either or both of paragraphs (a) and (c) in the case of a drug:
-- src:6354 | (a) to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer for that purpose;
-- src:6355 | (b) to immediately provide the samples of breath that, in the peace officer’s opinion, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made by means of an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer for that purpose;
-- src:6356 | (c) to immediately provide the samples of a bodily substance that, in the peace officer’s opinion, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made by means of approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer for that purpose.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.27(1) (src:6352-6356)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol or a drug in their body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` MEANS
    IF `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol or a drug in their body` AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that a person has alcohol or a drug in their body and that the person has, within the preceding three hours, operated a conveyance, the peace officer may, by demand, require the person"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.27(1)(b) (src:6352-6355)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol in their body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is an approved screening device, by s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` MEANS
    IF `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol in their body` AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the device is an approved screening device, by s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "either or both of paragraphs (a) and (b) in the case of alcohol"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.27(1)(c) (src:6352-6353)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has a drug in their body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is approved drug screening equipment, by s 320.11 the equipment is approved drug screening equipment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.27(1)(c) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer` MEANS
    IF `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has a drug in their body` AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the equipment is approved drug screening equipment, by s 320.11 the equipment is approved drug screening equipment` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "either or both of paragraphs (a) and (c) in the case of a drug"

-- (2): mandatory alcohol screening: no suspicion is required. "If a peace officer has in his or her possession an approved screening device, the peace officer may, in the course of the lawful exercise of powers
-- under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide the samples of breath".
-- src:6357 | Mandatory alcohol screening
-- src:6358 | (2) If a peace officer has in his or her possession an approved screening device, the peace officer may, in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide the samples of breath that, in the peace officer’s opinion, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made by means of that device and to accompany the peace officer for that purpose.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.27(2) (src:6357-6358)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has in their possession an approved screening device, by s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is operating a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` MEANS
    IF `the demand is made in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the officer has in their possession an approved screening device, by s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the person is operating a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a peace officer has in his or her possession an approved screening device, the peace officer may, in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle"

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.28: samples of breath or blood; evaluation; samples of bodily substances`

-- (1): "If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person has operated a conveyance while the person's ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol or has committed an offence under
-- paragraph 320.14(1)(b), the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, (a) require the person to provide, as soon as practicable, (i) the samples of breath ... approved instrument, or (ii) if the peace
-- officer has reasonable grounds to believe that ... the person may be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable ... the samples of blood ...; and (b) require the person to accompany".
-- src:6359 | Samples of breath or blood — alcohol
-- src:6360 | 320.28 (1) If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person has operated a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol or has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b), the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable,
-- src:6361 | (a) require the person to provide, as soon as practicable,
-- src:6362 | (i) the samples of breath that, in a qualified technician’s opinion, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made by means of an approved instrument, or
-- src:6363 | (ii) if the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that, because of their physical condition, the person may be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one, the samples of blood that, in the opinion of the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician taking the samples, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration; and
-- src:6364 | (b) require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of that person’s breath or blood.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(1) (src:6359-6364)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the technician is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` MEANS
    IF (`the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` OR `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)`)
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the instrument is an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the technician is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person has operated a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol or has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b), the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) (src:6359-6363)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that, because of their physical condition, the person may be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sample taker is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the sample taker is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` MEANS
    IF (`the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` OR `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)`)
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that, because of their physical condition, the person may be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND (`the sample taker is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` EQUALS (JUST TRUE) OR `the sample taker is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(ii) if the peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that, because of their physical condition, the person may be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one, the samples of blood"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(1)(b) (src:6359-6360)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of breath or blood` MEANS
    IF (`the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` OR `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)`)
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, ... (b) require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of that person’s breath or blood"

-- (2): the drug counterpart: "If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person has operated a conveyance while ... impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug, or has committed an offence
-- under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4), the peace officer may, by demand, made as soon as practicable, require the person to comply with ... (a) ... an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer ...; or (b) ... samples of blood".
-- src:6365 | Evaluation and samples of blood — drugs
-- src:6366 | (2) If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person has operated a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug, or has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4), the peace officer may, by demand, made as soon as practicable, require the person to comply with the requirements of either or both of paragraphs (a) and (b):
-- src:6367 | (a) to submit, as soon as practicable, to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer to determine whether the person’s ability to operate a conveyance is impaired by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug, and to accompany the peace officer for that purpose; or
-- src:6368 | (b) to provide, as soon as practicable, the samples of blood that, in the opinion of the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician taking the samples, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made to determine the person’s blood drug concentration, or the person’s blood drug concentration and blood alcohol concentration, as the case may be, and to accompany the peace officer for that purpose.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(2) (src:6365-6368)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evaluating officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` MEANS
    IF (`the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` OR `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)`)
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the evaluating officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person has operated a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug, or has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4), the peace officer may, by demand, made as soon as practicable"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(2)(b) (src:6365-6368)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sample taker is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the sample taker is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(2)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood and to accompany the peace officer` MEANS
    IF (`the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance while their ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` OR `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)`)
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the person making the demand is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND (`the sample taker is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` EQUALS (JUST TRUE) OR `the sample taker is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) to provide, as soon as practicable, the samples of blood that, in the opinion of the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician taking the samples"

-- (3): "An evaluating officer who has reasonable grounds to suspect that a person has alcohol in their body may, if a demand was not made under subsection (1), by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide,
-- as soon as practicable, the samples of breath that, in a qualified technician's opinion, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made by means of an approved instrument."
-- src:6369 | Samples of breath — alcohol
-- src:6370 | (3) An evaluating officer who has reasonable grounds to suspect that a person has alcohol in their body may, if a demand was not made under subsection (1), by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide, as soon as practicable, the samples of breath that, in a qualified technician’s opinion, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made by means of an approved instrument.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(3) (src:6369-6370)
GIVEN `the officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol in their body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a demand was not made under subsection 320.28(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the technician is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` MEANS
    IF `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol in their body` AND `a demand was not made under subsection 320.28(1)` AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the instrument is an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `the technician is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An evaluating officer who has reasonable grounds to suspect that a person has alcohol in their body may, if a demand was not made under subsection (1), by demand made as soon as practicable"

-- (4): "If, on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection (5) ... is impairing the person's ability to operate a conveyance,
-- the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question and may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide (a) a sample of oral fluid or urine ...; or (b) the samples of blood".
-- A duty (the officer shall identify) and two powers. The duty is JUST FALSE where its "if" is unmet.
-- src:6371 | Samples of bodily substances
-- src:6372 | (4) If, on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection (5) — or that a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs — is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance, the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question and may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide, as soon as practicable,
-- src:6373 | (a) a sample of oral fluid or urine that, in the evaluating officer’s opinion, is necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made to ascertain the presence in the person’s body of one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection (5); or
-- src:6374 | (b) the samples of blood that, in the opinion of the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician taking the samples, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made to ascertain the presence in the person’s body of one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection (5) or to determine the person’s blood drug concentration for one or more of those types of drugs.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(4) (src:6371-6374)
GIVEN `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs, is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(4) the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question` MEANS
    IF `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs, is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection (5) — or that a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs — is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance, the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question" (the "if" unmet)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(4)(a) (src:6371-6373)
GIVEN `the officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs, is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(4)(a) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide a sample of oral fluid or urine` MEANS
    IF `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs, is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance`
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question and may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide, as soon as practicable, (a) a sample of oral fluid or urine"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(4)(b) (src:6371-6374)
GIVEN `the officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs, is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sample taker is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the sample taker is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(4)(b) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` MEANS
    IF `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer has reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and one or more of those types of drugs, is impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance`
       AND `the demand is made as soon as practicable`
       AND `the officer is an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND (`the sample taker is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` EQUALS (JUST TRUE) OR `the sample taker is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) the samples of blood that, in the opinion of the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician taking the samples, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made to ascertain the presence in the person’s body of one or more of the types of drugs set out in subsection (5)"

-- (5): "For the purpose of subsection (4), the types of drugs are the following: (a) a depressant; ... (g) a narcotic analgesic." Read as closed ("are the following", a definition of the types; fork F12): any other type is JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `s 320.28(5) type of drug` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.28(5)(a) a depressant`
    `s 320.28(5)(b) an inhalant`
    `s 320.28(5)(c) a dissociative anaesthetic`
    `s 320.28(5)(d) cannabis`
    `s 320.28(5)(e) a stimulant`
    `s 320.28(5)(f) a hallucinogen`
    `s 320.28(5)(g) a narcotic analgesic`
    `s 320.28(5) a type of drug that is none of those`

-- src:6375 | Types of drugs
-- src:6376 | (5) For the purpose of subsection (4), the types of drugs are the following:
-- src:6377 | (a) a depressant;
-- src:6378 | (b) an inhalant;
-- src:6379 | (c) a dissociative anaesthetic;
-- src:6380 | (d) cannabis;
-- src:6381 | (e) a stimulant;
-- src:6382 | (f) a hallucinogen; or
-- src:6383 | (g) a narcotic analgesic.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(5) (src:6375-6383)
GIVEN `the type of drug` IS A `s 320.28(5) type of drug`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the type of drug`
    WHEN `s 320.28(5) a type of drug that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purpose of subsection (4), the types of drugs are the following"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (6): "A sample of blood may be taken from a person under this section only by a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician, and only if they are satisfied that taking the sample would not endanger the person's health."
-- src:6384 | Condition
-- src:6385 | (6) A sample of blood may be taken from a person under this section only by a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician, and only if they are satisfied that taking the sample would not endanger the person’s health.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(6) (src:6384-6385)
GIVEN `the person taking the sample is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person taking the sample is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person taking the sample is satisfied that taking the sample would not endanger the person’s health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person taking the sample is satisfied that taking the sample would not endanger the person’s health`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if they are satisfied that taking the sample would not endanger the person’s health"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: either holds` `the person taking the sample is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` `the person taking the sample is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only by a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician" (neither is one)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- (7): "A sample of blood shall be received into an approved container that shall be subsequently sealed." Whether the duty was met: a bare "shall" not done is JUST FALSE (fork F13).
-- src:6386 | Approved containers
-- src:6387 | (7) A sample of blood shall be received into an approved container that shall be subsequently sealed.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(7) (src:6386-6387)
GIVEN `the sample was received into an approved container, by s 320.11 the container is an approved container` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the container was subsequently sealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(7) the duty to receive the sample of blood into an approved container and to seal it has been met` MEANS
    IF NOT `the container was subsequently sealed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sample of blood shall be received into an approved container that shall be subsequently sealed" (the container was not sealed)
    ELSE `the sample was received into an approved container, by s 320.11 the container is an approved container`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE for a container that is not an approved container ("approved container means"); NOTHING when that is not covered

-- (8): "A person who takes samples of blood under this section shall cause one of the samples to be retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom the blood samples were taken."
-- src:6388 | Retained sample
-- src:6389 | (8) A person who takes samples of blood under this section shall cause one of the samples to be retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom the blood samples were taken.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(8) (src:6388-6389)
GIVEN `the samples of blood were taken under section 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the samples was retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom the blood samples were taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(8) the duty to cause one of the samples to be retained has been met` MEANS
    IF NOT `the samples of blood were taken under section 320.28`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who takes samples of blood under this section shall cause one of the samples to be retained" (no samples were taken under this section: the duty does not arise)
    ELSE JUST (`one of the samples was retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom the blood samples were taken`)

-- The party of the duty to retain a sample is "a person who takes samples of blood under this section" (by (6), a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician): the core's `Party` has no such
-- constructor, so this part declares one under its own prefix (NEEDS-CORE.md asks the lead to hoist it).
DECLARE `s 320.28 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.28 a person who takes samples of blood under section 320.28`

DECLARE `s 320.28(8) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.28(8) cause one of the samples of blood to be retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom they were taken`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(8) (src:6388-6389)
GIVEN `the samples of blood were taken under section 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 320.28 party` `s 320.28(8) action`
`s 320.28(8) the person who takes samples of blood shall cause one to be retained` MEANS
    IF `the samples of blood were taken under section 320.28`
    THEN PARTY `s 320.28 a person who takes samples of blood under section 320.28`
         MUST `s 320.28(8) cause one of the samples of blood to be retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom they were taken`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 320.28 a person who takes samples of blood under section 320.28` BECAUSE "no sample of blood was retained for the person from whom the samples were taken"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (9): "A failure to comply with subsection (7) or (8) does not by itself affect the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of the sample." Asks whether the failure alone affects validity.
-- src:6390 | Validity of analysis not affected
-- src:6391 | (9) A failure to comply with subsection (7) or (8) does not by itself affect the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of the sample.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(9) (src:6390-6391)
GIVEN `there was a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(9) a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8) by itself affects the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of it` MEANS
    IF `there was a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not by itself affect the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of the sample"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply with subsection (7) or (8)

-- (10): "A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of criminal jurisdiction shall, on the summary application of the person from whom samples of blood were taken under this section, made within six months
-- after the day on which the samples were taken, order the release of any sample that was retained to the person". A duty of the judge and the person's claim; the six months is a period the text fixes in its own words
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): outside it, JUST FALSE. Months are added with `Date`, which rolls an impossible day forward (fork F11).
-- src:6392 | Release of retained sample
-- src:6393 | (10) A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of criminal jurisdiction shall, on the summary application of the person from whom samples of blood were taken under this section, made within six months after the day on which the samples were taken, order the release of any sample that was retained to the person for the purpose of examination or analysis, subject to any terms that the judge considers appropriate to ensure that the sample is safeguarded and preserved for use in any proceedings in respect of which it was taken.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(10) (src:6392-6393)
GIVEN `the application is a summary application of the person from whom samples of blood were taken under section 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sample was retained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the samples were taken` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` MEANS
    IF `the application is a summary application of the person from whom samples of blood were taken under section 320.28` AND `a sample was retained`
       AND `the day on which the application is made` AT MOST (Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the samples were taken`) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the samples were taken` PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the samples were taken`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, on the summary application of the person from whom samples of blood were taken under this section, made within six months after the day on which the samples were taken, order the release of any sample that was retained"

DECLARE `s 320.28(10) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.28(10) order the release of the retained sample to the person, subject to any terms that the judge considers appropriate`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.28(10) (src:6392-6393)
GIVEN `the judge has received a summary application, made within six months, for the release of a retained sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.28(10) action`
`s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample` MEANS
    IF `the judge has received a summary application, made within six months, for the release of a retained sample`
    THEN PARTY `a judge`
         MUST `s 320.28(10) order the release of the retained sample to the person, subject to any terms that the judge considers appropriate`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the judge did not order the release of the retained sample"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.29: warrants to obtain blood samples`

-- (1): "A justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician to take the samples of a person's blood ... if the justice is satisfied, on an
-- information on oath in Form 1, that (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person has, within the preceding eight hours, operated a conveyance that was involved in an accident that resulted in
-- bodily harm to themselves or another person or in the death of another person; (b) ... reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol or a drug in their body; and (c) a qualified medical practitioner
-- is of the opinion that (i) ... the person is unable to consent ..., and (ii) the taking of samples ... will not endanger their health." A power of a justice: NOTHING when a gate is unmet.
-- src:6394 | Warrants to obtain blood samples
-- src:6395 | 320.29 (1) A justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician to take the samples of a person’s blood that, in the opinion of the practitioner or technician taking the samples, are necessary to enable a proper analysis to be made to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both, if the justice is satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1, that
-- src:6396 | (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person has, within the preceding eight hours, operated a conveyance that was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to themselves or another person or in the death of another person;
-- src:6397 | (b) there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol or a drug in their body; and
-- src:6398 | (c) a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that
-- src:6399 | (i) by reason of any physical or mental condition of the person, the person is unable to consent to the taking of samples of their blood, and
-- src:6400 | (ii) the taking of samples of the person’s blood will not endanger their health.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(1) (src:6394-6400)
GIVEN `the person who issues the warrant is a justice, by s 2 justice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding eight hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to the person or to another person, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol or a drug in their body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that, by reason of any physical or mental condition of the person, the person is unable to consent to the taking of samples of their blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that the taking of samples of the person’s blood will not endanger their health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` MEANS
    IF `the justice is satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1` AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person has operated a conveyance within the preceding eight hours`
       AND (`the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to the person or to another person, by s 2 bodily harm` EQUALS (JUST TRUE) OR `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person`)
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the person has alcohol or a drug in their body`
       AND `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that, by reason of any physical or mental condition of the person, the person is unable to consent to the taking of samples of their blood`
       AND `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that the taking of samples of the person’s blood will not endanger their health`
       AND `the person who issues the warrant is a justice, by s 2 justice` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician to take the samples of a person’s blood ... if the justice is satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1, that"

-- (2): "A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be in Form 5, varied to suit the case." The Form itself is a Form of the Code, after Part XXVIII (not in this range). Permission to use it: NOTHING outside a warrant under (1).
-- src:6401 | Form
-- src:6402 | (2) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be in Form 5, varied to suit the case.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(2) (src:6401-6402)
GIVEN `the warrant was issued under subsection 320.29(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.29(2) the warrant may be in Form 5, varied to suit the case` MEANS
    IF `the warrant was issued under subsection 320.29(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be in Form 5, varied to suit the case"

-- (3) is shown repealed in this text: "(3) [Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 10]". Row: repealed or blank in this text; carried as a constant that says what the text shows.
-- src:6403 | (3) [Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 10]
@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(3) (src:6403)
`s 320.29(3) as the text shows it` MEANS "(3) [Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 10]"

-- (4): "Samples of blood may be taken from a person under a warrant issued under subsection (1) only during the time that a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions referred to in subparagraphs
-- (1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist." Closed with "only".
-- src:6404 | Duration of warrant
-- src:6405 | (4) Samples of blood may be taken from a person under a warrant issued under subsection (1) only during the time that a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions referred to in subparagraphs (1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(4) (src:6404-6405)
GIVEN `a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions referred to in subparagraphs 320.29(1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.29(4) samples of blood may be taken from the person under the warrant at this time` MEANS
    IF `a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions referred to in subparagraphs 320.29(1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only during the time that a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions referred to in subparagraphs (1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist"

-- (5): "If a warrant issued under subsection (1) is executed, the peace officer shall, as soon as practicable, give a copy of it — as a well as a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case — to the person from whom the samples
-- of blood are taken." A duty of the peace officer and the person's claim; "as soon as practicable" states no number, so none is invented.
-- src:6406 | Copy to person
-- src:6407 | (5) If a warrant issued under subsection (1) is executed, the peace officer shall, as soon as practicable, give a copy of it — as a well as a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case — to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(5) (src:6406-6407)
GIVEN `the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is executed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a warrant issued under subsection (1) is executed, the peace officer shall, as soon as practicable, give a copy of it" (the "if" unmet)

DECLARE `s 320.29(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.29(5) give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case, to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(5) (src:6406-6407)
GIVEN `the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.29(5) action`
`s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give the person a copy of the warrant and a notice` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is executed`
    THEN PARTY `a peace officer`
         MUST `s 320.29(5) give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case, to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer` BECAUSE "the peace officer did not give the person a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (6): "Subsections 320.28(7) to (10) apply with respect to the taking of samples of blood under this section." A rule of application, limited to samples taken under a warrant of this section.
-- src:6408 | Taking of samples
-- src:6409 | (6) Subsections 320.28(7) to (10) apply with respect to the taking of samples of blood under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.29(6) (src:6408-6409)
GIVEN `the samples of blood are taken under section 320.29` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.29(6) subsections 320.28(7) to (10) apply to the taking of the samples of blood` MEANS
    IF `the samples of blood are taken under section 320.29`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to the taking of samples of blood under this section"

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.3: testing blood`

-- "Samples of a person's blood that are taken for the purposes of this Part may be analyzed to determine the person's blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both."
-- src:6410 | Testing blood — drug or alcohol
-- src:6411 | 320.3 Samples of a person’s blood that are taken for the purposes of this Part may be analyzed to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.3 (src:6410-6411)
GIVEN `the samples of the person’s blood were taken for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.3 the samples may be analyzed to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both` MEANS
    IF `the samples of the person’s blood were taken for the purposes of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Samples of a person’s blood that are taken for the purposes of this Part may be analyzed"
